00:53:55,159 --> 00:53:57,737
Anyway, you should search for Obata

813
00:53:57,873 --> 00:53:59,377
I don't have time to be doing that over here.

814
00:53:59,535 --> 00:54:01,823
Hey, why are you still so busy?

815
00:54:02,630 --> 00:54:06,905
Are you going out to chase women again?

816
00:54:06,930 --> 00:54:07,637
No.

817
00:54:08,148 --> 00:54:11,148
I am going to go shooting with President Nakazawa, I need to get ready

818
00:54:12,298 --> 00:54:14,534
With President Nakazawa, clay shooting?

819
00:54:14,559 --> 00:54:15,925
Are you jealous?

820
00:54:17,300 --> 00:54:18,191
Kamoi.

821
00:54:18,494 --> 00:54:22,018
Can you get me one of President Nakazawa's cigarette butts?

822
00:54:22,393 --> 00:54:23,128
Cigarette butts?

823
00:54:24,674 --> 00:54:25,525
Stupid detective.

824
00:54:26,879 --> 00:54:29,261
When it comes to clay shooting, it's a game for gentlemen, right?

825
00:54:29,286 --> 00:54:29,903
I know.

826
00:54:30,168 --> 00:54:31,535
It's an expensive and luxurious pastime

827
00:54:31,583 --> 00:54:33,739
Can you defy a gentleman?

828
00:54:34,122 --> 00:54:34,723
I can't.

829
00:54:34,926 --> 00:54:35,372
I can't.

830
00:54:36,824 --> 00:54:39,400
But it seems a bit strange

831
00:54:39,450 --> 00:54:40,979
This one is just too stiff

832
00:54:42,200 --> 00:54:43,504
There's a difference in the feel of steel and the water

833
00:54:45,137 --> 00:54:45,856
Pistol?

834
00:54:46,184 --> 00:54:46,739
No.

835
00:54:47,590 --> 00:54:49,230
You want the cigarette butt he smoked, don't you?

836
00:54:49,590 --> 00:54:51,956
Also, please ask the young lady about her blood type

837
00:54:52,237 --> 00:54:52,714
For what?

838
00:54:52,840 --> 00:54:53,752
Anything is fine

839
00:54:54,208 --> 00:54:56,247
You're really annoying.

840
00:54:59,540 --> 00:55:02,526
Is there something suspicious about President Nakazawa?

841
00:55:02,557 --> 00:55:04,025
That's the secret of the investigation.

842
00:55:04,581 --> 00:55:05,995
I see.

843
00:55:06,309 --> 00:55:07,004
Then I also.....

844
00:55:11,112 --> 00:55:13,034
You're really annoying.

845
00:55:13,589 --> 00:55:14,675
You are really....

846
00:55:14,848 --> 00:55:16,379
Someone who finds everything a hassle.

847
00:55:19,230 --> 00:55:21,416
Why do I have to take responsibility alone?

848
00:55:21,860 --> 00:55:24,046
Why did you try to team up with Kamoi?

849
00:55:24,192 --> 00:55:24,973
Just for business.

850
00:55:25,223 --> 00:55:25,911
Don't you lie.

851
00:55:27,208 --> 00:55:33,137
You tried to betray us by revealing the secret to Kamoi, the one you called the real deal

852
00:55:34,212 --> 00:55:37,212
You're trying to monopolize the new type of pistol all by yourself

853
00:55:37,938 --> 00:55:39,399
If you team up with me to take out the boss,

854
00:55:39,424 --> 00:55:40,770
there's a long way ahead

855
00:55:40,795 --> 00:55:41,931
How about you make up your mind,

856
00:55:41,956 --> 00:55:42,463
Bros!

857
00:55:42,488 --> 00:55:43,277
Shut up!

858
00:55:44,450 --> 00:55:45,559
Turn that way...

859
00:55:54,481 --> 00:55:55,440
You bastard!

860
00:56:09,504 --> 00:56:10,450
You bastard!

861
00:56:15,856 --> 00:56:16,778
You bastard!

862
00:56:39,676 --> 00:56:40,317
Boss?

863
00:56:42,293 --> 00:56:44,153
Take him way soon

864
00:56:58,027 --> 00:56:59,488
You're so great.

865
00:57:00,715 --> 00:57:01,348
Try this.

866
00:57:01,489 --> 00:57:02,379
Thank you very much.

867
00:57:05,348 --> 00:57:07,309
Using a large hunting gun is a good idea, too.

868
00:57:22,605 --> 00:57:24,160
It's truly magnificent

869
00:57:25,520 --> 00:57:27,582
It's a shame that I can't use unconventional shooting styles in clay pigeon shooting.

870
00:57:27,607 --> 00:57:28,434
unconventional shooting styles?

871
00:57:28,564 --> 00:57:29,610
Never mind

872
00:57:29,651 --> 00:57:30,456
Nakagawa-san.

873
00:57:32,001 --> 00:57:33,042
Excuse me for a moment

874
00:57:35,206 --> 00:57:36,955
It's your turn, young lady

875
00:57:36,980 --> 00:57:37,827
I wonder if it will go well.

876
00:57:51,331 --> 00:57:51,948
See you again.

877
00:57:51,973 --> 00:57:53,222
Thank you for your work.

878
00:58:35,831 --> 00:58:40,753
Nozaki-san, please determine the blood type from this cigarette butt.

879
00:58:40,955 --> 00:58:41,487
Yes

880
00:58:56,292 --> 00:58:56,956
Kimura-san

881
00:58:57,721 --> 00:59:02,323
Is it about the blood type of Nakazawa's deceased wife that
I received a request for over the phone earlier?

882
00:59:02,417 --> 00:59:03,488
Did you find anything?

883
00:59:03,963 --> 00:59:05,925
According to the hospital records, it was Blood O type.

884
00:59:05,964 --> 00:59:07,667
Blood O type?
Thank you very much.

885
00:59:09,600 --> 00:59:12,089
Yes, this is Kimura from the investigation headquarters

886
00:59:12,840 --> 00:59:15,066
The result of the analysis is type B

887
00:59:15,530 --> 00:59:18,206
Type B? Thank you very much.

888
00:59:25,550 --> 00:59:28,043
The young lady's blood type is A

889
00:59:29,190 --> 00:59:31,504
Ritsuko is type A, then you might be bad type.

890
00:59:31,895 --> 00:59:33,590
This is common knowledge.

891
00:59:35,684 --> 00:59:38,080
If the mother is type O and the father is type B,

892
00:59:38,464 --> 00:59:40,440
then a child with type A cannot be born

893
00:59:41,932 --> 00:59:44,190
Nakazawa is not Ritsuko's real father

894
00:59:45,170 --> 00:59:47,143
And about that leg injury...

895
01:00:03,901 --> 01:00:05,940
Please don't worry.

896
01:00:06,430 --> 01:00:07,866
Please

897
01:00:07,890 --> 01:00:08,723
About my father too

898
01:00:08,748 --> 01:00:09,793
I know

899
01:00:12,060 --> 01:00:13,105
Kamoi-san

900
01:00:13,262 --> 01:00:13,622
Take it

901
01:00:14,644 --> 01:00:15,262
What is this?

902
01:00:15,386 --> 01:00:17,434
This is a token of my appreciation for you.

903
01:00:17,997 --> 01:00:19,379
Don't mention it

904
01:00:19,606 --> 01:00:22,940
Don't worry,
I hope you like this

905
01:00:26,035 --> 01:00:27,316
See you then.

906
01:00:27,420 --> 01:00:28,582
Young lady?

907
01:00:34,911 --> 01:00:36,497
Thank you very much.

908
01:00:39,301 --> 01:00:40,075
Come in.

909
01:00:44,179 --> 01:00:45,199
Did you call for me?

910
01:00:50,700 --> 01:00:52,286
Please feed the piranhas.

911
01:01:16,430 --> 01:01:19,934
It seems that it's time.

912
01:01:21,130 --> 01:01:22,406
How is your injury?

913
01:01:22,504 --> 01:01:23,114
Not bad

914
01:01:23,754 --> 01:01:24,489
Not bad?

915
01:01:25,379 --> 01:01:28,045
Well, since I was hospitalized after injuring my arm,

916
01:01:28,070 --> 01:01:29,516
I have to stay until I recover

917
01:01:29,541 --> 01:01:30,590
That's right.

918
01:01:30,821 --> 01:01:32,962
Hospitals are places where wealthy people are found.

919
01:01:33,330 --> 01:01:34,041
I can't stand.

920
01:01:34,213 --> 01:01:35,502
Yes,you are right.

921
01:01:37,314 --> 01:01:38,604
What's that?

922
01:01:39,260 --> 01:01:40,072
The young lady gave me this.

923
01:01:40,830 --> 01:01:41,596
Who's the young lady?

924
01:01:41,908 --> 01:01:42,752
From Ritsuko.

925
01:01:46,703 --> 01:01:48,587
Oh wow, that's nice.

926
01:01:55,343 --> 01:01:56,634
Hey, that's nice

927
01:01:57,314 --> 01:01:58,338
Look at this.

928
01:02:00,021 --> 01:02:01,147
That's not good.

929
01:02:01,266 --> 01:02:02,532
I don't like the way you said that.

930
01:02:02,580 --> 01:02:04,346
I got injured because of you.

931
01:02:04,370 --> 01:02:05,026
So what?

932
01:02:05,050 --> 01:02:08,782
What would you do if I lost the use of my arm?

933
01:02:09,046 --> 01:02:10,852
What exactly are you trying to say?

934
01:02:13,759 --> 01:02:15,728
Don’t do that.

935
01:02:41,220 --> 01:02:42,134
Thank you, thank you

936
01:02:42,394 --> 01:02:44,212
Finally, I can stick to dinner with this

937
01:02:46,721 --> 01:02:49,291
What are you doing?
Are you drunk?

938
01:02:50,111 --> 01:02:51,432
You'll catch a cold if you go to sleep.

939
01:02:52,994 --> 01:02:54,799
You look pale.

940
01:02:57,838 --> 01:03:00,838
Blood!

941
01:03:03,041 --> 01:03:03,768
A fire might have broken out.

942
01:03:04,197 --> 01:03:04,713
Fire?

943
01:03:06,498 --> 01:03:08,478
Oh Stupid detective,
what are you doing!

944
01:03:08,869 --> 01:03:10,018
Blood!

945
01:03:11,369 --> 01:03:12,088
Stupid detective.

946
01:03:15,111 --> 01:03:15,588
Hey.

947
01:03:16,128 --> 01:03:17,494
What are you doing?
Call an ambulance

948
01:03:18,260 --> 01:03:19,244
Call an ambulance?

949
01:03:21,993 --> 01:03:23,349
Where did the fire break out?

950
01:03:25,049 --> 01:03:25,705
Where?

951
01:03:33,181 --> 01:03:34,775
Stupid detective.
You can't die!

952
01:03:35,580 --> 01:03:36,518
Shut up.

953
01:03:36,978 --> 01:03:38,028
Can you be a little quieter?

954
01:03:38,740 --> 01:03:41,259
You act superior.,
If this guy dies,I am angry with you guys.

955
01:03:41,770 --> 01:03:43,369
Does he need a blood transfusion?

956
01:03:43,394 --> 01:03:44,462
Using my blood

957
01:03:44,487 --> 01:03:45,303
I'll do anything!

958
01:03:45,641 --> 01:03:47,017
But that can wait until we go to the hospital

959
01:03:48,137 --> 01:03:51,455
This ambulance is slow. Hey, Drive faster.

960
01:03:51,709 --> 01:03:53,908
Stop it!
Don’t do that.

961
01:03:54,275 --> 01:03:55,283
Drive faster.

962
01:03:55,532 --> 01:03:56,830
Don't push it too hard,

963
01:03:56,929 --> 01:03:58,314
If you do that, we will take you out of the ambulance.

964
01:04:00,400 --> 01:04:01,338
Stupid detective.

965
01:04:01,518 --> 01:04:02,595
Have you regained consciousness?

966
01:04:02,620 --> 01:04:03,775
Don’t do that.

967
01:04:03,800 --> 01:04:04,595
Shut up.

968
01:04:10,681 --> 01:04:11,689
Nakazawa...

969
01:04:12,179 --> 01:04:13,400
What's wrong with him?

970
01:04:15,571 --> 01:04:16,375
Stupid detective.

971
01:04:19,369 --> 01:04:20,142
Stupid detective.

972
01:04:46,478 --> 01:04:47,463
Hurry up.

973
01:04:47,998 --> 01:04:50,494
I thought I could calm down a bit more,

974
01:04:50,874 --> 01:04:52,720
but it’s only been three years

975
01:04:53,150 --> 01:04:54,779
I'll say goodbye to Japan again

976
01:04:54,896 --> 01:04:56,243
Don’t complain

977
01:04:58,119 --> 01:04:59,658
I am not complaining.

978
01:05:00,090 --> 01:05:04,306
Have you forgotten how I picked you up from being a beggar while touring in America?

979
01:05:05,120 --> 01:05:06,361
Stop bringing up the past

980
01:05:06,890 --> 01:05:08,751
I should have done enough too

981
01:05:09,711 --> 01:05:12,711
During the day I'm a secretary, at night I'm your mistress

982
01:05:13,811 --> 01:05:15,634
But I'm already worn out.

983
01:05:17,300 --> 01:05:19,267
There are also good days

984
01:05:29,382 --> 01:05:30,556
What happened?

985
01:05:32,541 --> 01:05:34,057
Has something happened?

986
01:05:38,002 --> 01:05:39,314
What does this mean?

987
01:05:40,771 --> 01:05:42,025
You'll understand soon enough

988
01:05:44,054 --> 01:05:48,351
Father, it's something that you can't tell me?

989
01:05:53,570 --> 01:05:54,677
Oh, President

990
01:05:57,950 --> 01:05:58,587
How did it go?

991
01:05:59,040 --> 01:06:00,265
We killed the detective.

992
01:06:00,290 --> 01:06:01,072
He dead?

993
01:06:01,338 --> 01:06:02,127
He can't survive.

994
01:06:02,950 --> 01:06:03,966
Yumiko, hurry!

995
01:06:05,888 --> 01:06:08,470
After that, If you kill Kamoi, everything will be fine.

996
01:06:09,110 --> 01:06:14,486
Kamoi-san... Father... Please don't kill him

997
01:06:14,511 --> 01:06:15,471
Shut up!

998
01:06:16,153 --> 01:06:17,306
Don't say unnecessary things!

999
01:06:19,533 --> 01:06:20,744
Father...

1000
01:06:25,441 --> 01:06:27,220
Yes, this is the investigation headquarters

1001
01:06:29,393 --> 01:06:32,393
What!? Kimura-kun was shot!?

1002
01:06:36,870 --> 01:06:39,870
Stupid detective, it's my blood!

1003
01:06:40,270 --> 01:06:41,955
This is Daisuke Kamoi's blood

1004
01:06:42,880 --> 01:06:43,776
If it's not enough,

1005
01:06:43,800 --> 01:06:44,884
I will give you as much as you want.

1006
01:06:45,729 --> 01:06:46,432
Stupid detective.

1007
01:06:47,608 --> 01:06:56,814
I would be very lonely if you were gone.

1008
01:06:59,119 --> 01:06:59,807
Stupid detective.

1009
01:07:02,944 --> 01:07:03,908
Don't die

1010
01:07:07,869 --> 01:07:09,189
You can't die

1011
01:07:10,945 --> 01:07:13,712
The crime scene, at the Sakuraoka
Happiness Apartment in Shibuya,

1012
01:07:14,283 --> 01:07:17,266
Weapon was Molto
Gazelle X38,

1013
01:07:18,627 --> 01:07:19,986
We are launching an investigation.

1014
01:07:20,197 --> 01:07:20,799
Yes.

1015
01:07:33,038 --> 01:07:34,084
Stay strong.

1016
01:07:34,858 --> 01:07:35,663
Stay strong.

1017
01:07:38,389 --> 01:07:40,715
Doctor, please save him, okay?

1018
01:07:41,317 --> 01:07:42,357
I understand, I understand

1019
01:07:42,382 --> 01:07:43,834
You understand, right?

1020
01:07:45,014 --> 01:07:47,732
This is a lifelong request I have for you.

1021
01:07:47,757 --> 01:07:48,452
Nurse.

1022
01:07:49,197 --> 01:07:50,888
Let me ask you for one too

1023
01:07:55,701 --> 01:07:56,587
Stupid detective.

1024
01:07:57,061 --> 01:07:58,194
Have you regained consciousness?

1025
01:07:58,354 --> 01:07:58,814
You.

1026
01:08:00,369 --> 01:08:01,345
What did you just say?

1027
01:08:01,497 --> 01:08:03,470
Huh? What's wrong, Nakazawa?

1028
01:08:05,010 --> 01:08:06,049
Nakazawa is...

1029
01:08:07,876 --> 01:08:08,962
a fake!

1030
01:08:09,791 --> 01:08:10,674
What do you mean?

1031
01:08:12,234 --> 01:08:13,650
Is that really true?

1032
01:08:14,074 --> 01:08:19,337
He killed Ritsuko's father in America

1033
01:08:19,564 --> 01:08:20,955
He swapped places with him.

1034
01:08:21,667 --> 01:08:22,884
I see...

1035
01:08:24,732 --> 01:08:28,986
He tried to kill me because I found out about it.

1036
01:08:30,335 --> 01:08:34,251
The truth is, he's a notorious criminal named Suginami

1037
01:08:34,357 --> 01:08:37,638
Suginami? Is that how it was?

1038
01:08:39,174 --> 01:08:40,393
Yeah....

1039
01:08:42,572 --> 01:08:44,375
Let the investigation headquarters know

1040
01:08:44,400 --> 01:08:46,396
I understand, I understand. Don’t worry.

1041
01:08:47,091 --> 01:08:51,989
More importantly, you need to get better

1042
01:08:52,920 --> 01:08:53,478
Okay?

1043
01:08:53,503 --> 01:08:54,452
Now, please come out.

1044
01:09:04,665 --> 01:09:05,717
Stupid detective.

1045
01:09:06,521 --> 01:09:08,658
I will avenge you.

1046
01:09:12,666 --> 01:09:13,939
I will definitely do that.

1047
01:10:04,365 --> 01:10:05,026
Kamoi-san

1048
01:10:05,051 --> 01:10:06,029
What's wrong?

1049
01:10:06,443 --> 01:10:07,927
Nakazawa and the others have fled.

1050
01:10:08,148 --> 01:10:09,849
They put me through a terrible ordeal.

1051
01:10:10,123 --> 01:10:10,998
Where on earth did they go?

1052
01:10:11,208 --> 01:10:12,490
I don't know

1053
01:10:12,819 --> 01:10:15,715
Please protect me and let me escape

1054
01:10:15,834 --> 01:10:19,724
I'm scared...I'm scared...

1055
01:10:19,892 --> 01:10:23,013
But now that I've come,
it's okay. Don't worry

1056
01:10:24,724 --> 01:10:25,880
Kamoi-san.

1057
01:10:35,020 --> 01:10:37,142
I knew this would happen.

1058
01:10:39,760 --> 01:10:40,990
Guide me to Nagata's place

1059
01:10:42,503 --> 01:10:43,388
Hurry up.

1060
01:11:33,941 --> 01:11:34,916
Hurry up.

1061
01:11:35,142 --> 01:11:37,144
It's dangerous to go any faster, so I can't increase my speed.

1062
01:11:37,580 --> 01:11:38,638
I'm not talking to you

1063
01:11:39,287 --> 01:11:39,748
Hurry up.

1064
01:12:14,568 --> 01:12:15,908
Thank you for your patience.

1065
01:12:16,020 --> 01:12:17,456
We are ready,

1066
01:12:17,480 --> 01:12:19,111
so please prepare for the transaction

1067
01:12:30,693 --> 01:12:31,962
1 pistol 100,000 yen

1068
01:12:32,049 --> 01:12:32,627
What?

1069
01:12:33,716 --> 01:12:36,665
Please prepare 300,000 yen for one case

1070
01:12:36,960 --> 01:12:39,423
This differs from what we agreed upon.

1071
01:12:39,720 --> 01:12:40,876
This shouldn't be expensive

1072
01:12:41,450 --> 01:12:46,783
We put a great deal of effort into making this malt gazelle

1073
01:13:01,901 --> 01:13:02,970
Our boss is waiting.

1074
01:13:12,525 --> 01:13:13,174
Don't move!

1075
01:13:20,049 --> 01:13:21,666
Damn it.
Turn off the lights.

1076
01:14:08,340 --> 01:14:10,431
It's me.
where's the president?

1077
01:14:15,603 --> 01:14:16,498
Who's here?

1078
01:14:16,767 --> 01:14:17,571
Kamoi

1079
01:14:17,791 --> 01:14:18,283
He's alone?

1080
01:14:18,424 --> 01:14:18,854
Yes.

1081
01:14:19,430 --> 01:14:20,845
Don't let him get away!

1082
01:14:21,119 --> 01:14:22,447
kamoi is alone here.

1083
01:14:54,697 --> 01:14:55,423
This isn't good.

1084
01:14:56,634 --> 01:14:57,517
I can't see the fire,

1085
01:14:57,557 --> 01:14:59,376
I can't see where the enemy is.

1086
01:15:23,533 --> 01:15:24,408
Ritsuko.

1087
01:15:35,119 --> 01:15:35,775
Kamoi-san.

1088
01:15:38,775 --> 01:15:39,432
I feel scared.

1089
01:15:40,608 --> 01:15:43,384
Kamoi is with Ritsuko.
Surround them.

1090
01:15:43,729 --> 01:15:47,884
If we stay here, we'll be killed. we have to run and escape—no matter what.

1091
01:16:12,658 --> 01:16:15,275
Miss,  Nakazawa isn't your real father

1092
01:16:15,658 --> 01:16:16,212
I thought so

1093
01:16:16,237 --> 01:16:20,947
Well, that's because there was a criminal named Suginami
who killed your father in America and He swapped places with your father.

1094
01:16:24,751 --> 01:16:28,140
Upon learning that the police knew about it, he tried to kill Stupid detective and tried to escape.

1095
01:16:35,400 --> 01:16:36,118
Suginami.

1096
01:16:37,029 --> 01:16:38,946
Won't you face me in a contest?

1097
01:16:41,025 --> 01:16:42,017
Come on.

1098
01:16:42,790 --> 01:16:44,876
Kill two of them.

1099
01:16:50,040 --> 01:16:51,384
You have finally revealed your true colors.

1100
01:16:52,989 --> 01:16:54,587
Kill two of them.

1101
01:16:59,634 --> 01:17:00,056
Alright.

1102
01:17:00,880 --> 01:17:02,696
We can see him.
Go!

1103
01:17:16,305 --> 01:17:18,555
Young lady! Cross over to that platform!

1104
01:17:20,650 --> 01:17:21,642
Over there?

1105
01:17:21,730 --> 01:17:24,407
I'll do it first, so watch closely! Got it?

1106
01:17:29,692 --> 01:17:31,641
Young lady! Here! Got it?

1107
01:17:44,312 --> 01:17:46,227
If you stay here,
you'll be fine

1108
01:17:46,610 --> 01:17:47,649
How about you?

1109
01:17:49,579 --> 01:17:50,688
This brat.

1110
01:17:53,883 --> 01:17:55,922
I'm going to take revenge for Stupid detective.

1111
01:17:56,759 --> 01:18:01,297
Then I'm going to show you the pistol technique you said you wanted to see.

1112
01:18:03,410 --> 01:18:04,906
Come on, Suginami

1113
01:18:14,001 --> 01:18:15,258
I'll beat you!

1114
01:18:37,587 --> 01:18:38,821
Don't move,Kamoi.

1115
01:18:38,969 --> 01:18:41,141
Kill him!

1116
01:18:44,712 --> 01:18:45,407
Hurry up.

1117
01:18:48,165 --> 01:18:49,430
Let's get started!

1118
01:19:12,508 --> 01:19:13,485
Damn it.

1119
01:19:16,009 --> 01:19:17,923
We don't stand a chance of winning.

1120
01:19:20,673 --> 01:19:21,517
Let's do this.

1121
01:19:23,876 --> 01:19:25,032
Target that trunk.

1122
01:19:28,298 --> 01:19:30,329
Steal that trunk

1123
01:19:32,353 --> 01:19:33,900
Hurry up.

1124
01:19:37,407 --> 01:19:38,110
Damn it.

1125
01:19:44,696 --> 01:19:46,235
Take it away!

1126
01:19:51,267 --> 01:19:52,103
Hurry up.

1127
01:20:13,290 --> 01:20:15,285
Sugiyama, You should turn yourself in.

1128
01:20:15,310 --> 01:20:16,025
Shut up!

1129
01:20:16,543 --> 01:20:19,235
Our game is over.
You should turn yourself in.

1130
01:20:19,269 --> 01:20:20,315
What the heck!

1131
01:20:22,977 --> 01:20:23,579
Suginami.

1132
01:20:24,046 --> 01:20:26,423
There are only two rounds left in your pistol.

1133
01:20:29,580 --> 01:20:31,349
There are plenty of pistol rounds left.

1134
01:20:35,646 --> 01:20:36,466
Don't run away!

1135
01:20:43,629 --> 01:20:44,356
Ha!

1136
01:21:21,699 --> 01:21:23,074
Tsune-yan.

1137
01:21:23,337 --> 01:21:24,930
Tama-chan,What's wrong?

1138
01:21:25,172 --> 01:21:27,214
I was surprised when I read the newspaper.

1139
01:21:27,246 --> 01:21:28,772
I have returned from the tour.

1140
01:21:28,797 --> 01:21:32,042
I see, well, come on in and sit down

1141
01:21:33,411 --> 01:21:35,735
Um, well, Where's Kamoi-san?

1142
01:21:35,821 --> 01:21:36,868
He is out for a bit.

1143
01:21:37,000 --> 01:21:40,410
I see, um, How about Ritsuko-san?

1144
01:21:41,046 --> 01:21:44,557
She was not prosecuted.

1145
01:21:44,844 --> 01:21:45,646
What does that mean?

1146
01:21:46,024 --> 01:21:48,996
It means She did not become a criminal.

1147
01:21:49,300 --> 01:21:50,656
I see, that's great!

1148
01:21:50,960 --> 01:21:56,227
And usually, I think about this on the train when I'm coming back

1149
01:21:56,439 --> 01:21:58,102
I'll stop singing songs.

1150
01:21:58,455 --> 01:22:00,311
I thought I would become a wife.

1151
01:22:00,360 --> 01:22:00,969
You would become a wife?

1152
01:22:02,367 --> 01:22:03,826
That's nice.

1153
01:22:03,859 --> 01:22:05,185
That's nice.

1154
01:22:05,210 --> 01:22:06,178
So, with whom?

1155
01:22:06,562 --> 01:22:07,577
Well....

1156
01:22:08,700 --> 01:22:10,295
It's a bit embarrassing to say.

1157
01:22:13,136 --> 01:22:14,933
I'm embarrassed too.

1158
01:22:16,370 --> 01:22:17,660
I will cherish you.

1159
01:22:18,090 --> 01:22:19,090
Don't say stupid things.

1160
01:22:19,573 --> 01:22:21,206
I am not talking about you.

1161
01:22:21,501 --> 01:22:23,488
I am thinking of Kamoi-san.

1162
01:22:31,650 --> 01:22:33,133
The police chief?

1163
01:22:33,762 --> 01:22:34,809
Superintendent General of the Metropolitan Police Department

1164
01:22:36,817 --> 01:22:41,761
You are receiving a gift from a very distinguished person, aren't you?
I can't call you a stupid detective.

1165
01:22:43,087 --> 01:22:48,003
Since you’ve been praised in the newspaper, I can’t speak to you roughly like that.

1166
01:22:49,863 --> 01:22:51,012
Shall I call Kamoi-san and you now?

1167
01:22:52,605 --> 01:22:53,457
Kamoi-san

1168
01:22:54,074 --> 01:22:55,371
Kamoi-san?

1169
01:22:57,850 --> 01:22:59,972
It's kind of creepy

1170
01:23:00,553 --> 01:23:02,549
I feel like wearing a silk hat and tuxedo.

1171
01:23:02,616 --> 01:23:04,042
Call me Kamoi.

1172
01:23:04,090 --> 01:23:07,855
I see, so I guess I really like to be called stupid detective.

1173
01:23:07,880 --> 01:23:08,323
Yeah.

1174
01:23:10,678 --> 01:23:13,065
By the way, there's a great udon shop that opened

1175
01:23:13,224 --> 01:23:13,815
Is that true?

1176
01:23:13,847 --> 01:23:15,897
The udon there costs 30 yen.

1177
01:23:15,922 --> 01:23:17,053
That's cheap!

1178
01:23:17,310 --> 01:23:19,885
Next time I come to visit,
I'll bring you a souvenir.

1179
01:23:19,909 --> 01:23:20,306
Is that so?

1180
01:23:20,368 --> 01:23:21,521
Sorry about that, I appreciate it

1181
01:23:21,752 --> 01:23:22,404
By the way...

1182
01:23:24,420 --> 01:23:25,104
What?

1183
01:23:25,315 --> 01:23:26,198
Fee for the trouble of running the errand.

1184
01:23:26,650 --> 01:23:27,189
What?

1185
01:23:27,571 --> 01:23:28,866
I can offer you a special price—50 yen is fine.

1186
01:23:31,049 --> 01:23:32,792
You are a truly awful person.

1187
01:23:33,323 --> 01:23:34,612
You would be better off dead.

1188
01:23:56,687 --> 01:23:57,565
Young lady.

1189
01:24:20,745 --> 01:24:21,503
Young lady.

1190
01:24:23,244 --> 01:24:24,197
Hang in there.

1191
01:25:18,551 --> 01:25:26,843
THE END

